      "claim": "When the object is at infinity (do → ∞), the image distance di equals the focal length f.",
      "evidence": "Setting 1/do → 0 in the mirror equation gives 1/di = 1/f, so di = f.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "For any finite object distance do > f, the image distance di = (f·do)/(do – f); as do decreases toward f, di increases without bound.",
      "evidence": "Algebraic rearrangement of the mirror equation; denominator (do – f) → 0⁺ as do → f⁺, so di → +∞.",
