      "claim": "The linear magnification magnitude |m| = di/do = f/(do – f); as do → f⁺, |m| → ∞, so the image gets taller.",
      "evidence": "Definition of magnification for mirrors m = –di/do; substituting di from step 3 yields |m| = f/(do – f), which grows as the denominator shrinks.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [3]
    },
